I think your next milestone should be:

Resource-Constrained Resilience

Right now your recovery is effectively free:

\[
S_{t+1}=\min(S_{max},S_t+R)
\]

The system simply receives recovery_rate.

But eventually you want something closer to:

\[
R_t \leq E_t
\]

where \(E_t\) is available energy/resource capacity.

Then:

Threat
  ↓
Damage
  ↓
Recovery request
  ↓
Requires energy
  ↓
Energy decreases
  ↓
Recovery changes
  ↓
Repeated recovery becomes progressively harder

Now your reboot penalty also has somewhere to come from.

Instead of arbitrarily declaring:

reboot → -20% capacity

you can eventually model:

collapse
   ↓
reboot
   ↓
large energy expenditure
   ↓
thermal excursion
   ↓
structural degradation
   ↓
reduced capacity

That is the bridge from your abstract substrate toward a physically interpretable system.


